[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3]

; Dedicated fixture for the runtime INPUT-INJECTION lane — runtime_inject_input, the
; largest remaining gap on handoff 152 §2's ranked list (39 lines of GDScript, four `kind`
; branches plus bad_kind, of which the host unit tests reach exactly zero).
;
; THE FIXTURE QUESTION, ASKED FIRST — AND ANSWERED NO FOR THE FOURTH SESSION RUNNING.
; example/project.godot had no [input] section at all, so the `action` branch had nothing
; to be pointed at: Input.action_press on an unknown action is an engine error, not an
; injection. Two actions were added there for this fixture and this fixture only:
;
;   bp_probe_bound    -> ONE event, KEY_K, added by input_probe.gd's _ready() rather than
;                        serialised into project.godot — see that script's header, and note
;                        that this is not a style choice: the serialised form Godot 4.7
;                        writes carries `device: 16` and does NOT match an injected event on
;                        4.3 or 4.5, which cost this probe a red run on two of three arms.
;                        The bridge between the two lanes: a `key` injection carrying
;                        keycode 75 must show up BOTH as an InputEvent here and as this
;                        action going pressed, which is what proves the event went through
;                        the engine's real input pipeline rather than being handed straight
;                        to a listener.
;   bp_probe_unbound  -> NO events at all. The control. Nothing this probe injects may
;                        ever move it, so it is what makes "the key lane and the action
;                        lane are separable" a check rather than a hope — and it also
;                        proves `action` injection is pure InputMap state, since it can be
;                        pressed while having no binding that could produce it.
;
; ONE node, and it is an OBSERVER — see input_probe.gd. It never synthesises input. The
; reasoning is node_probe.tscn's, one step on: that lane's subject was the shape of the
; tree, so its fixture is scriptless; this lane's subject is whether an event ARRIVES, so
; its fixture may hold a script but that script must not be able to produce one.
;
; Deliberately NOT reusing an existing scene. Every other fixture here builds state in
; _ready() for its own lane, and three of them (verify_probe, anim_probe,
; peer_converge_probe) run timers or animations that would keep _input alive with traffic
; this probe would then have to subtract from its own counts.
;
; Driven headless by the runtime-plane CI job (:9087); see
; host/test-integration/inject-input.integration.mjs.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://tests/input_probe.gd" id="1_input"]

[node name="InputProbe" type="Node2D"]
script = ExtResource("1_input")
